  libvips-42.dll in the same package (dynamic, replaceable).
@img/sharp-wasm32 0.35.5 — Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later AND MIT: one
  WebAssembly module with libvips, glib, libexif and libheif (LGPL-3.0) and
  permissive libraries (resvg instead of librsvg; no cairo, pango or fribidi)
  compiled in, not separately replaceable. Its README lists them.
  Neither is installed on the supported hosts (Linux with glibc per ADR-0003,
  and macOS, as on the CI runners in .github/workflows/ci.yml): the win32 builds are
  Windows-only optional packages, and wasm32 is pulled in only by the
  FreeBSD and WebContainers sharp builds.
