Model weights (never committed; see models.lock.json)
YuNet and SFace are downloaded at runtime; FaceNet is built by an explicit command.
YuNet face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx — MIT.
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/opencv/face_detection_yunet
SFace face_recognition_sface_2021dec.onnx — Apache-2.0.
  Upstream: https://huggingface.co/opencv/face_recognition_sface
FaceNet facenet_inception_resnet_v1_vggface2.onnx (held-out model, ADR-0008) —
  built locally by each operator with `bun run models:export-facenet`, never
  downloaded from or redistributed by this project (ADR-0011).
  scripts/export-facenet.py exports it from:
  - facenet-pytorch 2.6.0 (code) — MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Timothy Esler.
    Upstream: https://github.com/timesler/facenet-pytorch
    Installed only into the export script's own uv environment, with its
    pinned PyTorch, ONNX and ONNX Runtime; none of it ships with Iconograph.
  - Pretrained weights 20180402-114759 (Inception-ResNet-v1, trained on
    VGGFace2) by David Sandberg, published in an MIT repository, Copyright (c)
    2016 David Sandberg (https://github.com/davidsandberg/facenet, LICENSE.md;
    the README is silent on separate terms for the weights). Ported to
    PyTorch by facenet-pytorch (also MIT, no separate terms for the weights):
    https://github.com/timesler/facenet-pytorch/releases/download/v2.2.9/20180402-114759-vggface2.pt
  - Training data: the VGGFace2 dataset (Oxford Visual Geometry Group;
    Q. Cao, L. Shen, W. Xie, O. M. Parkhi, A. Zisserman, "VGGFace2: A dataset
    for recognising faces across pose and age", FG 2018,
    https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.08092). Its terms, checked 2026-11-01 in the
    Internet Archive (the live page no longer offers the data):
    dataset page, 2019-02-21
    (http://web.archive.org/web/20190221052714/http://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/vgg_face2/):
    "The VGGFace2 dataset is available to download for commercial/research
    purposes under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    License. The copyright remains with the original owners of the image."
    Its licence file
    (http://web.archive.org/web/2019/http://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/vgg_face2/files/licence_vggface2.txt):
    "The dataset is covered under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International license." and "Downloading this dataset implies agreement
    to follow the same conditions for any modification and/or
    re-distribution of the dataset in any form." Oxford VGG has since
    withdrawn the download links. How these terms apply to weights trained
    on the data is unsettled; this project therefore chooses not to
    redistribute the weights or its export, and credits VGGFace2 as above.

Test fixtures
-------------
packages/adapters/test/fixtures/faces/ holds public-domain works of the US
federal government via Wikimedia Commons (PD-USGov-POTUS, PD-USGov-NASA):
portraits by White House staff photographers David Lienemann (2013),
Adam Schultz (2021, 2022) and Pete Souza (2012, 2015), and NASA's Apollo 17
Earth photograph, plus one generated plain-grey HEIC. Source URLs, authors and
local modifications are listed in that folder's README.md. Personality rights
of the people shown are unaffected; the images are used only as test data and
imply no endorsement.

